## Highlights
The ECL from a redox-active MOF prepared from \(\{\mathsf{R u}[4,4^{\prime}\cdot(\mathsf{H O}_{2}\mathsf{C})_{2}\mathrm{-}\mathsf{b p y}]_{2}\mathsf{b p y}\}^{2+}\) and \(Z\mathsf{n}^{2+}\) was reported.
The redox-activity and well-ordered porous structure of the MOF were confirmed by its electrochemistry and ECL emission.
The MOF exhibited permselectivity, charge selectivity, and catalytic selectivity.
A stable and concentration-dependent ECL emission was observed toward co-reactants.
